{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "A Wildcard Hero prestiges its active specialization at Chromie and can buy its scrolls back at the level cap",
  "contract": "On Darkmoon - Season 10 Wildcard a Hero at level 60 could prestige at Chromie (178081). The client's Prestige window (AscensionUI/Gossips/PrestigeMode.lua) says for Wildcard: 'Resets your CURRENT SPECIALIZATION ONLY. This is a complete reset of all abilities. Slot new Skillcards on your run to unlock your build. Resets your current specializations Scroll of Fortune quest chain.', and its confirmation deletes the Scrolls of Fortune, Cases of Fortune and Bonus Manastorm Caches of that specialization from bags and bank. The window lists those scrolls as REPURCHASEABLE from SMSG 0x720 words 8-10 (scrolls, ability scrolls, talent scrolls), sent before Chromie's gossip. After the reset the character is level 1 with the Prestige Challenge aura 9930831 and an empty build that gets the starting choice again, cannot switch specialization until the level cap, and holds the Prestige rewards (100000 Runes of Ascension 375250) and the achievement Prestige 1 (13100) with its title '%s I' (CharTitles 200; Prestige 2-9 give '%s II'-'%s IX', Prestige 10 'The Prestigious %s'). The deleted scrolls, redeemed tokens included, become the specialization's repurchasable counts in SMSG 0x6EE/0x6EF; at the level cap CMSG 0x6F1/0x6F2/0x6F3 {u32 count, u8 gold} buys them back for 50/50/33 Runes of Ascension each (or 20/20/15 gold), answered by SMSG 0x6F4 REPURCHASE_WILDCARD_ROLL_OK or the reason, e.g. NOT_MAX_LEVEL.",
  "timeout_ms": 180000,
  "location": {"map": 0, "x": -8816.5, "y": 627.0, "z": 94.1, "o": 3.8},
  "players": [
    {"id": "wild", "race": 1, "class": 10, "level": 60}
  ],
  "creatures": [
    {"id": "chromie", "owner": "wild", "entry": 178081, "distance": 2, "faction": 35}
  ],
  "steps": [
